WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.233
Everything on Deliveries.

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:11.000
Deliveries. The drivers' week (instead of the Google Calendar and the whiteboard) and every dumpster: where it is and who has it.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:15.033
Pick the week. The arrows go back or forward a week.

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:24.300
New run. Books a material delivery, or a container drop, pickup, swap or move. Tour: "Book a delivery or container run".

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.600
Runs today. Runs still to do today, and which drivers have them.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.933
This week. All the runs this week and how many are done.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:40.167
Containers out. Containers at customers, out of all of them; the rest are in the yard.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:52.067
Full or late. Containers the customer says are full, waiting for pickup. With none, it counts late runs: earlier days not done, also listed in a red banner.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:01:02.100
The drivers' week. A row per driver, a column per day (Sunday only when a run is on it). Not assigned holds runs with no driver yet.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:12.167
A run. Time, container number, customer, and what it is with the truck. The edge colour is the kind of run; done runs are faded with a tick.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:20.633
Drag to move. Drag a run to another day or driver to move it; the driver's phone follows. Done runs stay put.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.367
Add a run on a day. The + in a day starts a run for that driver and day.

00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:30.233
Open a run. Click a run to see all of it.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:39.167
The details. What, when, driver, truck, customer, address, container, job, load and notes; once done, who did it and when.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:43.400
Edit. Changes the run (the same form as New run).

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:51.867
Mark done. For when the driver couldn't on the phone. A drop asks which container went out; the container moves with the run.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.933
Cancel run. Cancels the run (it asks first).

00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:59.100
Customer. Opens the customer.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.267
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving anything.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:12.667
Container yard. Every dumpster / roll-off: its number, size, where it is and what's next. Tour: "Track dumpsters".

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.800
Out. Containers at customers, full ones too.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.467
Yard. Ready to go.

00:02:19.967 --> 00:02:22.200
Repair. Out of service.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.933
All. Back to all of them.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:30.033
Add container. A new dumpster: its number, size and notes.

00:02:30.533 --> 00:02:41.867
A container. Size, number, status (In the yard, Out, Full · pickup due, Repair), customer and address, days out and the next run. Click it for history and actions.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:47.967
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
